  1	## Design System
  2	
  3	Apply these defaults. They are opinionated and tested — override only when user requests it.
  4	
  5	### Design Notes
  6	- **Use inline SVG for icons, NOT emojis.** Simple path-based SVGs for a professional look. See the Icons section above.
  7	- **Chart.js charts MUST be destroyed and recreated on theme toggle** — not just CSS variable swaps. Colors are read at render time, so the chart must be rebuilt with new computed values.
  8	- **Chart.js: DISABLE default animation** — Add `Chart.defaults.animation = false;` before creating charts. Default animations cause charts to appear blank/broken in screenshots, Playwright tests, and initial renders. This is a recurring bug that caused "broken charts" in rounds 13-25.
  9	- **Chart.js: Use explicit color values** — Don't concatenate CSS variable values with hex alpha suffixes (e.g., `c.remote + '18'`). Use explicit `rgba()` values instead: `'rgba(12, 206, 107, 0.15)'`.
 10	- **Chart.js: Don't use resetCanvas** — Just reuse the same canvas element. Destroy the old chart instance with `.destroy()` then create a new one on the same canvas.
 11	- **Chart.js: Build after layout is stable** — Use `window.addEventListener('load', ...)` with a short `setTimeout(200)` and trigger `window.dispatchEvent(new Event('resize'))` after building.
 12	
 13	### Typography
 14	- **Primary font:** Inter via Google Fonts CDN — `/app/libs/fonts/inter.css`
 15	- **Professional letter-spacing (Apple/Stripe-inspired):**
 16	  - **Hero headings (h1):** `letter-spacing: -0.03em` — tight like Apple keynote titles
 17	  - **Section headings (h2-h3):** `letter-spacing: -0.02em`
 18	  - **Body text:** `letter-spacing: -0.011em` for refined readability
 19	  - **Labels/caps:** `letter-spacing: 0.05em` for small uppercase text
 20	  - **Font features:** `font-feature-settings: 'cv11', 'ss01';` for Inter's stylistic alternates
 21	- **Font-weight hierarchy (Stripe-inspired):**
 22	  - **h1:** `font-weight: 700` (bold, not 800 — optically cleaner at large sizes)
 23	  - **h2:** `font-weight: 600` (semibold)
 24	  - **Card titles:** `font-weight: 600`
 25	  - **Body text:** `font-weight: 400` (regular)
 26	  - **Labels:** `font-weight: 500` (medium)
 27	- **Text colors (Vercel-inspired):** Never pure white. Use `#ededed` or `var(--text)` which maps to `#f5f5f7` in dark mode. Secondary text at 60% opacity feel (`#888` or `var(--text-secondary)`)
 28	- **NO gradient text on headings** — use solid colors only. Gradient text looks cheap at scale.
 29	- **Multilingual support:** When content includes non-Latin text (Korean, Japanese, Chinese, etc.), add the appropriate Google Fonts:
 30	  - **Korean:** Noto Sans KR — `/app/libs/fonts/noto-sans-kr.css`
 31	  - **Japanese:** Noto Sans JP — `/app/libs/fonts/noto-sans-jp.css`
 32	  - **Chinese (Simplified):** Noto Sans SC — `/app/libs/fonts/noto-sans-sc.css`
 33	  - **Arabic:** Noto Sans Arabic — `/app/libs/fonts/noto-sans-arabic.css`
 34	  - Set `font-family: 'Noto Sans KR', 'Inter', sans-serif;` (CJK font first, then Inter fallback for numbers/Latin)
 35	  - Set `<html lang="ko">` (or appropriate language code)
 36	- **Custom fonts:** When the user requests a specific font or vibe:
 37	  - **Serif/editorial:** Lora, Playfair Display, Source Serif Pro
 38	  - **Monospace/code:** JetBrains Mono, Fira Code, Source Code Pro
 39	  - **Display/creative:** Space Grotesk, Outfit, Sora, Poppins
 40	  - **Handwritten:** Caveat, Patrick Hand
 41	  - Fonts are pre-installed at `/app/libs/fonts/`. Use `<link href="/app/libs/fonts/inter.css" rel="stylesheet">`
 42	  - Update the `--font-primary` CSS var and `body { font-family: ... }` accordingly
 43	- **Light mode text optimization:** Use softer text colors, not harsh black:
 44	  - Primary text: `#1a1a1a` (not #000000) for better readability
 45	  - Secondary text: `#666666` for proper hierarchy
 46	  - Never pure black text on white backgrounds - it's too harsh
 47	- **Font detection:** Infer the right font from context:
 48	  - Korean/Japanese/Chinese content → auto-add Noto Sans KR/JP/SC
 49	  - Code-heavy content (cheat sheets) → add JetBrains Mono for code blocks
 50	  - Formal/editorial content → consider a serif font for headings
 51	  - Playful/creative content → consider display fonts
 52	- **Monospace:** JetBrains Mono or system `'SF Mono', 'Fira Code', 'Consolas', monospace`
 53	- **Fallback:** `-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif`
 54	- **Type scale (dramatic):** Make hero titles bigger, body should breathe more — 14 → 16 → 20 → 25 → 31 → 39 → 49px
 55	- **Line-height:** 1.5–1.7 for body, 1.1 for headings (tight for professional feel)
 56	- **Max line width:** 65–75 characters for readability
 57	- Use `clamp()` for fluid responsive sizing: `clamp(1rem, 2.5vw, 1.25rem)`
