 59	### Modern CSS Techniques (Chrome 105+)
 60	
 61	Use these cutting-edge CSS features where supported for better UX:
 62	
 63	**Popover API** (Chrome 114+) — Zero-JS tooltips, info panels, and modals:
 64	```html
 65	<button popovertarget="info-panel">ℹ Details</button>
 66	<div id="info-panel" popover>
 67	  <h3>More Information</h3>
 68	  <p>Details shown on click, no JS needed.</p>
 69	</div>
 70	```
 71	```css
 72	[popover] {
 73	  background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border);
 74	  border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px; max-width: 320px;
 75	  box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
 76	}
 77	[popover]::backdrop { background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3); }
 78	```
 79	Use for: dashboard metric details, architecture node info, chart annotations.
 80	
 81	**Exclusive `<details>` Accordion** (Chrome 120+) — Collapsible sections, no JS:
 82	```html
 83	<details name="faq" open><summary>Section 1</summary><p>Content</p></details>
 84	<details name="faq"><summary>Section 2</summary><p>Content</p></details>
 85	```
 86	Same `name` attribute = only one open at a time. Use for: cheatsheets, process guides, FAQs, any content with collapsible groups.
 87	
 88	**`::details-content` Styling** (Chrome 131+) — Animate accordion open/close:
 89	```css
 90	details { overflow: hidden; }
 91	::details-content {
 92	  transition: block-size 0.3s ease, opacity 0.3s ease;
 93	  block-size: 0; opacity: 0;
 94	}
 95	details[open]::details-content {
 96	  block-size: auto; opacity: 1;
 97	}
 98	```
