153	### Color System (Class-Based Theming — NO @media prefers-color-scheme)
154	
155	**CRITICAL: Do NOT use `@media (prefers-color-scheme)` for theme variables.** It fights with class-based `.theme-dark`/`.theme-light` and causes themes to break when OS mode differs from selected theme. Use ONLY class-based selectors on `html`:
156	
157	```css
158	/* Theme via class on <html> — JS detects prefers-color-scheme on first load */
159	html.theme-dark {
160	  --bg: #0A0A0A;              /* near-black (Linear-inspired) */
161	  --surface: #141414;          /* barely lighter than bg */
162	  --surface-hover: #1C1C1C;
163	  --border: rgba(255,255,255,0.04);  /* nearly invisible borders */
164	  --text: #EDEDED;             /* not pure white */
165	  --text-secondary: #888888;
166	  --accent: #3b82f6;
167	  --accent-secondary: #8b5cf6;
168	  --positive: #10b981;
169	  --negative: #f43f5e;
170	  --warning: #f59e0b;
171	  --info: #06b6d4;             /* semantic info color */
172	  --muted: #0f0f0f;            /* subtle backgrounds */
173	}
174	html.theme-light {
175	  --bg: #FAFAF9;               /* warm off-white */
176	  --surface: #FFFFFF;
177	  --surface-hover: #F5F5F4;
178	  --border: #e5e5e5;           /* more visible than 0.06 opacity */
179	  --text: #1a1a1a;             /* softer than pure black */
180	  --text-secondary: #666666;   /* better contrast than #64748b */
181	  --accent: #2563eb;
182	  --accent-secondary: #7c3aed;
183	  --positive: #059669;
184	  --negative: #e11d48;
185	  --warning: #d97706;
186	  --info: #0ea5e9;             /* semantic info color */
187	  --muted: #f8fafc;            /* subtle backgrounds */
188	}
189	```
